# Binary diagnostics (AoC 2021 Day 3) — the classic bit-counting puzzle:
# gamma takes each column's majority bit, epsilon its complement; report
# gamma * epsilon.
#
# Transpose turns columns into rows; each row's sum against the line count
# (12 here) decides the majority; frombin reads the assembled bit string.
#
#   domain challenges/06_binary_diagnostics.domain
Cursed Energy: 06_binary_diagnostics.input
Shikigami: Digit Grid
Cursed Technique: Transpose
Cursed Technique: Apply
    Using: (g) -> list(sum(row(g, 0)), sum(row(g, 1)), sum(row(g, 2)), sum(row(g, 3)), sum(row(g, 4)))
Cursed Technique: Map Each
    Using: (s) -> if 2 * s > 12 then "1" else "0"
Maximum Technique: Join with ""
Cursed Technique: Apply
    Using: (s) -> frombin(s) * (31 - frombin(s))
Reveal: stdout
